 176:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c **** /**
 177:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   * @brief  Update SystemCoreClock variable according to Clock Register Values.
 178:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *         The SystemCoreClock variable contains the core clock (HCLK), it can
 179:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *         be used by the user application to setup the SysTick timer or configure
 180:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *         other parameters.
 181:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *
 182:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   * @note   Each time the core clock (HCLK) changes, this function must be called
 183:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *         to update SystemCoreClock variable value. Otherwise, any configuration
 184:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *         based on this variable will be incorrect.
 185:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *
 186:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   * @note   - The system frequency computed by this function is not the real
 187:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *           frequency in the chip. It is calculated based on the predefined
 188:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *           constant and the selected clock source:
 189:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *
 190:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is HSI, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSI_VALUE(**)
 191:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *
 192:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is HSE, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSE_VALUE(***)
 193:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *
 194:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is PLL, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSE_VALUE(***)
 195:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *             or HSI_VALUE(*) multiplied/divided by the PLL factors.
 196:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *
 197:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *         (**) HSI_VALUE is a constant defined in stm32g4xx_hal.h file (default value
 198:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *              16 MHz) but the real value may vary depending on the variations
 199:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *              in voltage and temperature.
 200:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *
 201:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *         (***) HSE_VALUE is a constant defined in stm32g4xx_hal.h file (default value
 202:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *              24 MHz), user has to ensure that HSE_VALUE is same as the real
 203:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *              frequency of the crystal used. Otherwise, this function may
 204:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *              have wrong result.
 205:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *
 206:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *         - The result of this function could be not correct when using fractional
 207:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *           value for HSE crystal.
 208:stm/stm32g4xx/system_stm32g4xx.c ****   *
